WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.920
The 2010s were full of capes and tights on
the big screen, and as we look back on the

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.240
past ten years, it’s time to discuss the
best superhero movies of the last decade.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.299
Even after the first trailer hit, The Avengers,
a movie with multiple superheroes teaming

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.680
up on the big screen, felt like something
that couldn't possibly work.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.600
Then the film arrived, and it was an absolute
blast.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.380
The Avengers is certainly not a perfect film,
but it inspired a sense of awe simply by existing

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.860
and being as fully formed and solid as it
was.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.020
There's a certain miraculous quality to that
particular team-up, helmed with humor and

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.000
heart by writer-director Joss Whedon , that
makes it feel magical.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.690
Avengers movies are a pop culture language
all their own now, but back then, it was hard

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.000
to imagine something like this working so
well.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.260
That it still works nearly a decade later
is proof that The Avengers was a certain kind

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.320
of lightning in a bottle.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:55.480
"The idea was to bring together remarkable
people to see if they could become something

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:55.980
more."

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.960
To this day, The Dark Knight Rises is a particularly
divisive film among superhero fans.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.380
Still, the thing that sticks out years after
its release is Nolan's inarguable sense of

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.320
scope and ambition.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.420
Where The Dark Knight was often at its best
when it functioned as a psychological duel

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:16.330
between two opposing personalities, The Dark
Knight Rises was epic in its scale and its

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:16.820
themes.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.840
The film is practically operatic in its sensibility.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.240
It remains the boldest, broadest, most daring
portion of the Dark Knight trilogy, and the

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.640
gutsy swings it took are still worth revisiting.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.960
"Now we came here not as conquerers but as
liberators, to return control of this city

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.640
to the people."

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:41.080
Deadpool famously spent years in development
as star Ryan Reynolds lobbied for an R-rated

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.940
superhero comedy that would break the fourth
wall and mock everything from the X-Men movies

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:45.940
to Green Lantern.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.440
Even after it was finally greenlit, questions
surrounded Deadpool's ability to execute its

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.660
meta style for the full length of a feature
film.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.360
When the film finally arrived, it put all
those questions to rest.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.900
The movie was a full-blown phenomenon, led
by Ryan Reynolds' obvious glee in the title

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.520
role, and it proved there was an appetite
for more R-rated superhero fare.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:08.680
Hugh Jackman had been wearing the claws as
Wolverine for nearly 20 years by the time

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.440
he decided to make Logan his curtain call
as the character.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.640
Jackman's final Wolverine effort could've
been a glorified cameo in another massive

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:16.400
X-Men film.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.920
Instead, he and director James Mangold made
sure the character went out like an old gunslinger

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.840
in a futuristic, superhero Western.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.480
From the opening sequence to the heart-wrenching
final act, Logan is the kind of masterpiece

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.660
every franchise actor hopes to go out on.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:34.560
With Wonder Woman, director Patty Jenkins
and star Gal Gadot gave us a dynamic, fierce

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.860
film that followed Diana from her childhood
to her first great battle among mortals.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:42.800
The film is packed with instantly memorable
sequences, from the "No Man's Land" battle

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:47.020
that became its centerpiece to Diana and Steve
Trevor's slow-burning romance.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:51.540
Meanwhile, the supporting cast, led by an
absurdly charming Chris Pine, make sure that

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.600
even the quieter scenes are fun to watch.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.060
Even now, Wonder Woman still stands as the
DC Extended Universe's very best film.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:00.940
"You did this."

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.100
"We did."

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:10.720
Thor: Ragnarok gave the god of thunder the
kind of boundless science fiction overtones

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.940
that he's often had in his comic book adventures.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:17.440
The film also threw in an added extra dose
of comedy to underline Thor's place among

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.080
the most lovably well-intentioned idiots in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.960
Director Taika Waititi's visual stamp, from
the brightly colored sets to the oddly shaped

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.620
spaceships, is all over the film.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:32.120
Ragnarok is proof that even the most established
franchise heroes can still be refreshed with

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:32.920
new blood.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:37.940
There was a lot riding on Black Panther, the
first superhero film in the mega-popular Marvel

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.560
Cinematic Universe to feature a black lead
character and a primarily black leading cast.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:47.160
Everyone wanted it to change the world, but
they also wanted a great superhero blockbuster.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.840
With the deck stacked against them, director
Ryan Coogler and his cast managed to do both.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.060
With its Oscar-winning score, costumes, and
production design, the movie tapped into a

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.880
culture and mythology rarely seen in Hollywood
movies.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:03.299
Plus, it gave us one of the best supervillains
to ever grace the silver screen Michael B.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.900
Jordan as the deadly yet sympathetic Erik
Killmonger.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.900
"These items aren't for sale."

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.680
"How do you think your ancestors got these?

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.150
Think they paid a fair price?

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.500
Or did they take it like they took everything
else?"

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.040
Black Panther absolutely changed the superhero
genre, and it's the kind of film that will

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.120
remain a touchstone of the genre for years
to come.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.640
If there's one superhero who's arguably oversaturated
the big screen in the 21st century, it's Spider-Man.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.400
Then Into the Spider-Verse arrived and quickly
proved that there's no such thing as too much

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.580
Spider-Man if you know what you're doing.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.640
The film's dynamic and endlessly compelling
animation style, killer voice cast, and moving

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:42.720
story combined to create what might just be
the best Spider-Man movie to date.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:47.020
It's a film that understands the Spider-Man
journey with such precision that it can communicate

00:04:47.029 --> 00:04:50.080
vast emotional truths in the span of a single
moment.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.340
You leave the theater believing that anyone
really can wear the mask.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:58.500
Directed by Julia Hart, Fast Color tells the
intimate story of a family, the strange powers

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.040
they keep, and the troubles that have kept
them at a distance from one another in a dying

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.320
world where it hasn't rained in years.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.680
Gugu Mbatha-Raw leads a fantastic small ensemble
of actors as they navigate the tense emotional

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.270
landscape of a story that's as much about
family ties as it is about superpowers.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:19.140
Tense, well-crafted and full of heart, Fast
Color is a masterclass in how to use genre

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.940
conventions judiciously.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:26.080
It builds and builds in a patient, careful
way right up until a deeply emotionally satisfying

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:26.800
climax.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:31.639
In a landscape full of mega-franchises, it's
a reminder that there should be room for smaller

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:35.420
films like this, because they can often hit
us just as hard as the blockbusters.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.420
The concluding film in what Marvel Studios
dubbed "the Infinity Saga," Avengers: Endgame

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:44.640
is like Infinity War in that it's a sprawling
ensemble piece with the fate of the universe

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:45.140
at stake.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:49.080
Beyond that, though, the two films diverge
in a number of powerful ways.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:53.580
Endgame was a sure thing at the box office,
but that didn't stop the team behind it from

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:58.441
taking any number of risks, including an early
death scene, a major time jump, and of course,

00:05:58.441 --> 00:06:01.580
a time-traveling caper that takes up a big
chunk of the film.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:06.119
It's a swing for the fences with a massive
payoff that covers not just the three-hour

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.580
film but the entire previous decade of filmmaking
at Marvel.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:13.680
"This is the fight of our lives and we're
going to win.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:17.700
Whatever it takes."

